weakspot.news.1.9.4=Clearer name for the stats average; logo in the Mods list
weakspot.news.1.9.3=Internal cleanup (no gameplay changes)
weakspot.news.1.9.2=Chat notice when a new version is out
weakspot.news.1.9.0=Servers can now turn off mining, growth, machine and animal spots (not compatible with 1.8.x)
weakspot.news.1.8.9=Every config option now has an English description, plus internal cleanup
weakspot.breed.line=Breeding: %s
weakspot.breed.separator= / 
weakspot.breed.ready=Ready to breed (it starts after a short wait)
weakspot.breed.no_village=Not in a village (needs houses with doors)
weakspot.breed.not_season=A villager died nearby; no breeding for a while
weakspot.breed.doors=Not enough doors (%s villagers, %s doors; %s more needed)
weakspot.breed.cooldown=Cooldown %s left
weakspot.breed.cooldown.boost=Cooldown %s left (hits speed it up)
weakspot.breed.food=Not enough food (3 bread, or 12 carrots or potatoes)
weakspot.breed.no_mate=No partner nearby
weakspot.breed.mate_child=The nearest partner is a child
weakspot.breed.mate_cooldown=The partner is on cooldown
weakspot.breed.mate_food=The partner lacks food
# 設定画面の説明（1.8.9 で、それまで @Config.Comment だけだった項目にも足した）
weakspot.server.mining.boostmultiplier.tooltip=[Server] Mining speed multiplier after a hit (the extra part is also scaled by the combo factor)
weakspot.server.mining.boostdurationticks.tooltip=[Server] How long the multiplier lasts (ticks). One hit digs (multiplier - 1) x this many ticks' worth
weakspot.server.mining.weakspotradiusratio.tooltip=[Server] Weak spot radius (ratio to the shorter side of the face)
weakspot.server.mining.edgemargin.tooltip=[Server] Minimum gap between the weak spot and the edge of the face (blocks)\nLarger values keep spots near the center; too large shortens how far they move
weakspot.server.mining.minmovedistance.tooltip=[Server] Minimum distance a weak spot moves after a hit (blocks)
weakspot.server.mining.weakspotminradius.tooltip=[Server] Minimum weak spot radius (blocks), so small faces like buttons stay hittable\nThe maximum (weakSpotMaxRadiusRatio) wins if they conflict
weakspot.server.mining.weakspotmaxradiusratio.tooltip=[Server] Maximum weak spot radius (ratio to the shorter side), so spots stay inside small faces
weakspot.server.mining.minfacesize.tooltip=[Server] Shortest side a face needs for a weak spot (blocks). Smaller faces (carpet sides, etc.) get none\n0 shows spots on any face
weakspot.server.mining.lingerticks.tooltip=[Server] How long a weak spot stays after you stop holding (ticks)
weakspot.server.mining.minhitintervalticks.tooltip=[Server] Minimum interval between accepted mining hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way
weakspot.server.repair.hitsperrepair.tooltip=[Server] When you break a block, every this many mining hits on it repairs the held tool\nHits on blocks you did not break do not count. The remainder carries over. 0 disables repair
weakspot.server.repair.repairperstep.tooltip=[Server] Durability repaired per hitsPerRepair
weakspot.server.repair.maxrepairperbreak.tooltip=[Server] Maximum durability repaired per broken block. Anything above is dropped\n0 disables repair (milestone rewards still apply)
weakspot.server.milestones.milestones.tooltip=[Server] Total mining hits that count as milestones. Each gives a celebration and rewards once\nmilestoneXp and milestoneRepair follow this order. Per-kind milestones use the same numbers
weakspot.server.milestones.milestonexp.tooltip=[Server] Experience for each milestone (same order as milestones)\nMissing entries count as 0
weakspot.server.milestones.milestonerepair.tooltip=[Server] Durability repaired on the held tool for each milestone (same order as milestones; mining only)\nMissing entries count as 0
weakspot.server.milestones.milestonerepeatinterval.tooltip=[Server] After the largest milestone, a milestone every this many hits. 0 stops repeating\nThe reward is the last milestoneXp / milestoneRepair value
weakspot.server.milestones.kindmilestonesenabled.tooltip=[Server] Also give milestones for each kind other than mining, using the milestones numbers\nThe reward is experience only (milestoneXp)
weakspot.server.milestones.totalmilestonesenabled.tooltip=[Server] Also give milestones for the total hits of all kinds (numbers in totalMilestones)
weakspot.server.milestones.totalmilestones.tooltip=[Server] Total hits of all kinds that count as total milestones\ntotalMilestoneXp follows this order
weakspot.server.milestones.totalmilestonexp.tooltip=[Server] Experience for each total milestone (same order as totalMilestones)\nMissing entries count as 0
weakspot.server.milestones.totalmilestonerepeatinterval.tooltip=[Server] After the largest total milestone, one every this many hits. 0 stops repeating\nThe reward is the last totalMilestoneXp value
weakspot.server.growth.growthticksperhit.tooltip=[Server] Extra random ticks given to a crop or sapling per growth hit\nUnlike bone meal, growth conditions such as light and farmland moisture still apply
weakspot.server.growth.growthwarnings.tooltip=[Server] Tell the player in chat when growth hits do not make a plant grow\nToo dark (light below 9 for crops, stems and saplings): on the first hit; otherwise after growthStuckHits hits without change
weakspot.server.growth.growthstuckhits.tooltip=[Server] Hits without any change before warning that something else stops the plant from growing
weakspot.server.growth.growthminhitintervalticks.tooltip=[Server] Minimum interval between accepted growth hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way
weakspot.server.growth.growthminradius.tooltip=[Server] Minimum radius of growth weak spots (blocks), so small faces stay hittable
weakspot.server.growth.growthexcludedblocks.tooltip=[Server] Block IDs that never get growth weak spots (also applies to sugar cane, cactus and nether wart)\nBy default, blocks with IGrowable that are not crops (grass block, grass, ...) are excluded
weakspot.server.growth.mushroomgrowchance.tooltip=[Server] Chance (0-1) that one growth hit on a mushroom tries to grow a huge mushroom (same as one bone meal)\nVanilla conditions apply; if it fails, the mushroom stays
weakspot.server.growth.growthextrablocks.tooltip=[Server] Extra blocks that get growth weak spots; hits give them extra random ticks\nOne per line: "id" or "id[property=condition,...]". Conditions: 0-6 (range), dry_* (* matches anything), or an exact value\nExample: somemod:crop[age=0-6]. Without conditions it always shows (nether wart defaults to age=0-2, ic2:rubber_wood to state=dry_*;\nsugar cane and cactus height is checked in code). Do not add blocks that use random ticks for other things (leaves, grass, farmland, ice)\nBlocks in growthExcludedBlocks are excluded even if listed here
weakspot.server.machine.machineboostmultiplier.tooltip=[Server] How many times per tick update() runs on a hit machine (4.0 = 3 extra calls per tick)\nIf several players boost the same machine, the larger value is used, not the sum
weakspot.server.machine.machineboostmaxmultiplier.tooltip=[Server] Maximum machine multiplier. Also sent to clients (the "Machine Nx speed" label). Combos multiply machineBoostMultiplier\n(x1.25 at 25, x1.5 at 50, x2 at 100, x2.5 at 250, x3 at 500, x4 at 1000), capped by this value\nLower it if a machine mod misbehaves or the server is under load. It wins even when below machineBoostMultiplier
weakspot.server.machine.machineboostparticles.tooltip=[Server] Show colored particles around boosted machines (visible to nearby players,\nexcept those who turned machineParticlesVisible off). Server only (not sent to clients)
weakspot.server.machine.machineboostdurationticks.tooltip=[Server] How long a machine boost lasts (ticks). At machineMinHitIntervalTicks or more, hitting at the fastest pace never lets it drop
weakspot.server.machine.machineminhitintervalticks.tooltip=[Server] Minimum interval between accepted machine hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way
weakspot.server.machine.excludedblocks.tooltip=[Server] Block IDs that machines boosting ignores. Sneaking with an empty hand opens their GUI as usual\nAdd machines that break when boosted
weakspot.server.animal.animalbabyenabled.tooltip=[Server] Animal weak spots speed up babies growing up
weakspot.server.animal.animalbreedingenabled.tooltip=[Server] Animal weak spots shorten the breeding cooldown
weakspot.server.animal.sheepwoolenabled.tooltip=[Server] Sheep weak spots regrow wool faster (no grass needed)
weakspot.server.animal.chickeneggenabled.tooltip=[Server] Chicken weak spots shorten the time to the next egg
weakspot.server.animal.villagertraderesetenabled.tooltip=[Server] Villager weak spots reset the limits of locked trades
weakspot.server.animal.animalbabyhits.tooltip=[Server] About how many hits turn a baby into an adult (one hit = 24000 ticks / this)\n0 or less disables it
weakspot.server.animal.animalbreedinghits.tooltip=[Server] About how many hits end the breeding cooldown (one hit = 6000 ticks / this)\n0 or less disables it
weakspot.server.animal.sheepwoolhits.tooltip=[Server] Hits for a sheared sheep to regrow its wool\n0 or less disables it
weakspot.server.animal.chickenegghits.tooltip=[Server] About how many hits until the next egg (one hit = 9000 ticks on average / this)\n0 or less disables it
weakspot.server.animal.villagertraderesethits.tooltip=[Server] Hits to reset the limits of a villager's locked trades\n0 or less disables it
weakspot.server.animal.animalminhitintervalticks.tooltip=[Server] Minimum interval between accepted animal hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way
weakspot.server.animal.animalexcludedentities.tooltip=[Server] Entity IDs that never get animal weak spots (e.g. minecraft:cow)\nRight clicking them works as usual
weakspot.server.animal.animalsneakrequiredentities.tooltip=[Server] Modded animal entity IDs that only show weak spots while sneaking with an empty hand\nAdd animals whose empty-hand right click does something else (ride, open an inventory, sit). Vanilla horses, tamed wolves, etc. are handled in code
weakspot.server.animal.villagerresetunlocksnewtier.tooltip=[Server] Resetting a villager's trade limits also unlocks a new trade tier (like vanilla restocking)\nOff: only unlocks locked trades. Server only (not sent to clients)
weakspot.server.fishing.fishingweakspotenabled.tooltip=[Server] Turn the fishing weak spots on or off
weakspot.server.fishing.fishinghits.tooltip=[Server] Hits that cut the longest wait (600 ticks) to zero (one hit = 600 ticks / this)\n0 or less disables fishing weak spots
weakspot.server.fishing.fishingminhitintervalticks.tooltip=[Server] Minimum interval between accepted fishing hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way
weakspot.server.bow.bowweakspotenabled.tooltip=[Server] Turn the bow weak spots on or off
weakspot.server.bow.bowhitticks.tooltip=[Server] Ticks of bow draw added per hit (a vanilla bow is fully drawn after 20 ticks)\nNever goes past full draw. 0 disables bow weak spots
weakspot.server.bow.bowminhitintervalticks.tooltip=[Server] Minimum interval between accepted bow hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way
weakspot.server.sleep.sleepweakspotenabled.tooltip=[Server] Turn the sleeping weak spots on or off\nWhile sleeping at night, a marker shows on the sleep screen. Clicking it moves the world time forward (for everyone)
weakspot.server.sleep.sleephitticks.tooltip=[Server] World time added per sleeping hit (ticks). Never goes past the next morning\nServer only (not sent to clients)
weakspot.server.sleep.sleepminhitintervalticks.tooltip=[Server] Minimum interval between accepted sleeping hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way
weakspot.server.eat.eatweakspotenabled.tooltip=[Server] Turn the eating and drinking weak spots on or off\nWhile eating or drinking, a weak spot shows near the crosshair. Hits shorten the time to finish
weakspot.server.eat.eathitticks.tooltip=[Server] Ticks removed from eating or drinking per hit. Vanilla food takes 32 ticks, so 16 finishes in 2 hits
weakspot.server.eat.eatminhitintervalticks.tooltip=[Server] Minimum interval between accepted eating hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way
weakspot.server.vehicle.vehicleweakspotenabled.tooltip=[Server] Turn the vehicle weak spots on or off\nWhile riding a moving horse, pig, minecart or boat, a weak spot shows near the crosshair. Hits speed it up for a while
weakspot.server.vehicle.vehicleboostmultiplier.tooltip=[Server] Vehicle speed multiplier after a hit, scaled by the combo factor (x1.25 at 25 ... x4 at 1000)
weakspot.server.vehicle.vehicleboostmaxmultiplier.tooltip=[Server] Maximum vehicle speed multiplier. 0 means no limit (default; x6 at combo 1000)\nSet 3.0 or so if it gets too fast
weakspot.server.vehicle.vehicleboostdurationticks.tooltip=[Server] How long a vehicle boost lasts (ticks). Each hit resets it
weakspot.server.vehicle.vehicleminhitintervalticks.tooltip=[Server] Minimum interval between accepted vehicle hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way
weakspot.server.ladder.ladderweakspotenabled.tooltip=[Server] Turn the ladder weak spots on or off\nWhile climbing a ladder or vines, a weak spot shows straight above or below the crosshair. Hits speed up climbing for a while
weakspot.server.ladder.ladderboostmultiplier.tooltip=[Server] Climbing speed multiplier after a hit, scaled by the combo factor (x1.25 at 25 ... x4 at 1000)
weakspot.server.ladder.ladderboostmaxmultiplier.tooltip=[Server] Maximum climbing speed multiplier. 0 means no limit (default)\nSet 3.0 or so if it gets too fast
weakspot.server.ladder.ladderboostdurationticks.tooltip=[Server] How long a climbing boost lasts (ticks). Each hit resets it
weakspot.server.ladder.ladderminhitintervalticks.tooltip=[Server] Minimum interval between accepted ladder hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way
weakspot.server.elytra.elytraweakspotenabled.tooltip=[Server] Turn the elytra weak spots on or off\nWhile flying with an elytra, a weak spot shows near the crosshair. Hits launch you where you look
weakspot.server.elytra.elytraboostpower.tooltip=[Server] Speed added per elytra hit (blocks/tick), scaled by the combo factor\nNo speed limit
weakspot.server.elytra.elytraminhitintervalticks.tooltip=[Server] Minimum interval between accepted elytra hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way
weakspot.server.enchant.enchantweakspotenabled.tooltip=[Server] Turn the enchanting weak spots on or off\nWith an item on an enchanting table, a marker shows on the screen. Clicking it rerolls the three offers (costs nothing)
weakspot.server.enchant.enchantminhitintervalticks.tooltip=[Server] Minimum interval between accepted enchanting hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way
weakspot.server.harvest.harvestweakspotenabled.tooltip=[Server] Turn the harvest weak spots on or off\nHolding right click with an empty hand on a ripe crop shows a weak spot. Hits harvest and replant it\nTurn it off if another mod (such as Quark) already harvests on right click
weakspot.server.harvest.harvestminhitintervalticks.tooltip=[Server] Minimum interval between accepted harvest hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way
weakspot.server.harvest.harvestcombobonus.tooltip=[Server] Multiply harvest drops by the combo factor (x1.25 at 25 ... x4 at 1000; seeds are not multiplied)\nServer only (not sent to clients)
weakspot.server.throw.throwweakspotenabled.tooltip=[Server] Turn the throwing weak spots on or off\nWhile holding ender pearls, snowballs, eggs, potions or bottles o' enchanting, a weak spot shows near the crosshair\nEach hit charges up; the next throw flies faster and farther (kept until you switch items, used up when thrown)
weakspot.server.throw.throwchargeperhit.tooltip=[Server] Charge added per throwing hit (added to the throw speed multiplier), scaled by the combo factor\nNo charge limit
weakspot.server.throw.throwminhitintervalticks.tooltip=[Server] Minimum interval between accepted throwing hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way
weakspot.server.sprint.sprintweakspotenabled.tooltip=[Server] Turn the sprint weak spots on or off\nWhile sprinting on the ground, a weak spot shows straight above or below the crosshair. Hits make you run faster for a while
weakspot.server.sprint.sprintboostmultiplier.tooltip=[Server] Sprint speed multiplier after a hit, scaled by the combo factor (x1.25 at 25 ... x4 at 1000)
weakspot.server.sprint.sprintboostmaxmultiplier.tooltip=[Server] Maximum sprint speed multiplier. 0 means no limit (default)\nSet 3.0 or so if it gets too fast
weakspot.server.sprint.sprintboostdurationticks.tooltip=[Server] How long a sprint boost lasts (ticks). Each hit resets it
weakspot.server.sprint.sprintminhitintervalticks.tooltip=[Server] Minimum interval between accepted sprint hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way
weakspot.server.melee.meleeweakspotenabled.tooltip=[Server] Turn the melee weak spots on or off\nWhile holding a sword or axe near enemies, weak spots show left and right of the crosshair. Each hit charges up the next attack
weakspot.server.melee.meleeminhitintervalticks.tooltip=[Server] Minimum interval between accepted melee hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way
weakspot.server.melee.meleechargeperhit.tooltip=[Server] Charge added per melee hit (added to the next attack multiplier), scaled by the combo factor\nA charged attack is a critical hit (x1.5) and then x(1 + charge)
weakspot.server.melee.meleechargemax.tooltip=[Server] Maximum melee charge. 0 means no limit (default)\nSet 2.0 or so if it gets too strong
weakspot.server.portal.portalweakspotenabled.tooltip=[Server] Turn the nether portal weak spots on or off\nWhile standing in a portal, a weak spot shows near the crosshair. Hits shorten the wait before you travel
weakspot.server.portal.portalhitticks.tooltip=[Server] Portal wait removed per hit (ticks), scaled by the combo factor. The vanilla wait is 80 ticks
weakspot.server.portal.portalminhitintervalticks.tooltip=[Server] Minimum interval between accepted portal hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way
weakspot.server.swim.swimweakspotenabled.tooltip=[Server] Turn the swim weak spots on or off\nWhile swimming, a weak spot shows near the crosshair; hitting it gives a short dash and faster swimming for a while
weakspot.server.swim.swimboostmultiplier.tooltip=[Server] Swim speed multiplier after hitting the swim weak spot, with the combo factor on top. Keep it the same as the vehicle multiplier so boats stay faster
weakspot.server.swim.swimboostmaxmultiplier.tooltip=[Server] Cap on the swim speed multiplier. 0 means no cap
weakspot.server.swim.swimboostdurationticks.tooltip=[Server] How long the swim boost lasts (ticks). Each hit resets it to this length
weakspot.server.swim.swimdashdistance.tooltip=[Server] How far the dash on a swim hit carries you (blocks, roughly). Combos do not make it longer
weakspot.server.swim.swimminhitintervalticks.tooltip=[Server] Minimum interval between accepted swim hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way
weakspot.server.melee.critsperrepair.tooltip=[Server] Every this many landed charged melee attacks repair the held item. 0 disables it\nThe remainder carries over until logout. Server only (not sent to clients)
weakspot.server.melee.critrepairperstep.tooltip=[Server] Durability repaired per critsPerRepair. Server only (not sent to clients)
weakspot.server.general.giveguidebook.tooltip=[Server] Give players a guide book on their first login (once per player)\nIt can also be read with the Guide button on the stats screen (K key). Server only (not sent to clients)
weakspot.server.general.markersharerange.tooltip=[Server] Range for relaying other players' weak spot markers (blocks). Only players within this distance of a marker see it\n0 stops relaying (other players' markers are not shown)
weakspot.server.general.markersendminintervalticks.tooltip=[Server] Minimum interval between marker updates sent per player (ticks). Keeps network traffic down
weakspot.client.sound.myhitsound.tooltip=[Client] Note block instrument for your hit sound\nXYLOPHONE, CHIME, BELL, FLUTE, GUITAR, HARP, BASS, HAT, SNARE, BASEDRUM, PLING\nAlso on the Sound tab of the stats screen (K key), with a preview
weakspot.client.sound.myhitvolume.tooltip=[Client] Volume of your hit sound (0 is silent)\nThe vanilla Players volume also applies
weakspot.client.sound.hitchordenabled.tooltip=[Client] Stack notes on your hit sound as your combo grows (2 notes from 25, 3 from 100). Off keeps a single note
weakspot.client.sound.othershitvolume.tooltip=[Client] Volume of other players' hit sounds (0 is silent)\nThe vanilla Players volume also applies
weakspot.client.sound.othershitsound.tooltip=[Client] Note block instrument for other players' hit sounds\nXYLOPHONE, CHIME, BELL, FLUTE, GUITAR, HARP, BASS, HAT, SNARE, BASEDRUM, PLING
weakspot.client.markers.othermarkerenabled.tooltip=[Client] Show other players' weak spot markers
weakspot.client.markers.othermarkercolor.tooltip=[Client] Color of other players' weak spot markers (#RRGGBB). Pick one you can tell from your own\nInvalid values use the default light blue #3FA9FF
weakspot.client.markers.othermarkeralpha.tooltip=[Client] Opacity of other players' markers (multiplied with your own marker's; 1 is the same, 0 is invisible)
weakspot.general.configversion.tooltip=[Internal] Config file migration version. Do not edit
weakspot.server.mining.miningweakspotenabled.tooltip=[Server] Turn the mining weak spots on or off\nOff: nobody gets mining weak spots (vanilla mining)
weakspot.server.mining.miningcombobonus.tooltip=[Server] Turn the mining combo bonus on or off\nOn: each hit digs more as the combo grows (x1.25 at 25 ... x4 at 1000)
weakspot.server.growth.growthweakspotenabled.tooltip=[Server] Turn the crop and sapling growth weak spots on or off\nOff: nobody gets them, and empty-hand right clicks work as usual
weakspot.server.machine.machineweakspotenabled.tooltip=[Server] Turn the machine weak spots on or off\nOff: nobody gets them, and sneaking with an empty hand opens the GUI as usual
weakspot.server.animal.animalweakspotenabled.tooltip=[Server] Turn the animal weak spots on or off\nOff: nobody gets them, and empty-hand right clicks work as usual
